# Applies to every build whose context is the repo root: the control-plane (needs
# control-plane/ + the top-level policies/ seed), BOTH sandbox tiers (claude-sandbox/
# and opencode-sandbox/, each of which also needs the shared sandbox-common/ scripts),
# and both UIs, the control-plane UI and the tasks UI (each its own directory + the
# shared ui-common/). The sandbox images use a root context precisely so they can COPY
# sandbox-common/ — a build context cannot reach outside itself, and the firewall must
# have ONE implementation, not a copy per tier; the UIs' reason is the same for
# ui-common/. The egress proxy, tool-gateway and task-registry build from their own
# directories, unaffected.
#
# Keep the root context small: exclude anything no root-context image needs.
.git
.github
proxies
tests
models
run-claude-sandbox.sh
run-opencode-sandbox.sh
sandbox-lib.sh
Makefile
# Root only, on purpose: the sandbox Dockerfiles COPY their user-*.md files.
*.md
.env
.hadolint.yaml
.shellcheckrc
.yamllint
# Bytecode is written beside every module, so **/ (any depth), not a bare name (root only).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.ruff_cache
# Host-local state that the Makefile keeps OUT of the tree by default, listed for the
# hand-run case that lands it here anyway. Nothing COPYs these today, and the point
# is that a future `COPY . .` cannot start to.
backups
secrets
# Claude Code's project directory: agent worktrees and local settings, and the repo's
# own skills and agents, which are instructions for a session, never image content.
.claude
